WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:06.300
Adam needs a new phone and cannot decide between two models.

2
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:08.950
Który telefon jest lepszy?

3
00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:12.240
Ten jest szybszy i ma lepszy aparat.

4
00:00:12.890 --> 00:00:14.050
A tamten?

5
00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.820
Tamten jest tańszy, ale ma mniejszy ekran.

6
00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:26.410
Faster, better, cheaper, smaller: four comparatives in two sentences.

7
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.780
W takim razie wezmę ten tańszy.

8
00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:35.410
Ten telefon jest tańszy niż tamten.

9
00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:40.010
The comparative adds an ending to the adjective.

10
00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:44.600
The superlative puts three more letters in front of it.

11
00:00:44.950 --> 00:00:50.230
The most common adjectives are irregular, so learn them as pairs.

12
00:00:52.430 --> 00:00:54.910
Ask which one is better.

13
00:00:57.410 --> 00:00:59.010
Który jest lepszy?

14
00:00:59.810 --> 00:01:03.370
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

15
00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:06.770
Który jest lepszy?

16
00:01:08.770 --> 00:01:12.810
This is the best café in town. Say it.

17
00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:18.030
To jest najlepsza kawiarnia w mieście.

18
00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:22.390
Did you say it? Say it once more, out loud.

19
00:01:24.190 --> 00:01:26.910
To jest najlepsza kawiarnia w mieście.

20
00:01:28.910 --> 00:01:32.470
Now practise with the exercises below the video.
